    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as our anchor; his score of 75.76 against Kolek is the highest on the board, driven by a favorable SP_xERA of 4.36 and a prime #3 hole assignment. Close behind him, **Lars Nootbaar** offers our best value opportunity (67.77) due to a highly exploitable matchup against Waldrep (7.82 xERA). Both **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** are strong starts in the 63-65 range against Jones; while the pitcher\u2019s metrics are moderate, their batting order proximity in the #1 and #2 slots provides the run-scoring upside necessary to maintain our pace in this 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's docket was the exclusion of **Dillon Dingler**. With a score of 36.28, he fell just shy of our 40-point floor; despite an impressive xwOBA of 0.386, his unfavorable platoon split against Eovaldi and the defensive pressure of the opposing pitcher's ability to hold runners pushed him to the pine. Elsewhere, we are leaning into platoon advantages with **Christian Yelich** and **Luke Raley**, both of whom benefit from positive splits despite facing sub-5.00 xERA arms. As we monitor the rest of the roster\u2014including the status of **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, both sidelined today\u2014we must remain vigilant regarding the defensive capabilities of opposing batteries, as our reliance on **Trea Turner** for stolen base production remains the critical engine of our efficiency.",
